-- issue #1493: an interface METHOD named for a prelude standalone that the PRELUDE'S
-- OWN BODIES CALL (`identity`, stdlib/core.mdk:1432, called at :842 `flat x = andThen x
-- identity`, :979, :981, :1157, :1214) makes core.mdk itself ill-typed. All three verbs
-- reject at exit 1 with diagnostics about PRELUDE INTERNALS -- `Bimappable`'s `mapFirst`
-- and `mapSecond` default bodies -- located at THIS file's line 1.
--
-- Nothing below mentions Bimappable, mapFirst, mapSecond, or the type variables the
-- diagnostics quote. Crucially, nothing below applies `identity` to an `Int`, yet the
-- last diagnostic demands `No impl of Idn for Int`: that obligation can only have been
-- raised by an occurrence of `identity` inside a PRELUDE body.
--
-- Hand-derived correct answer: this program is legal and prints 7 (see control.mdk,
-- which is this file with the method renamed and which prints exactly that).
interface Idn c where
  identity : c -> Int

data Box = Box Int

impl Idn Box where
  identity (Box n) = n

main = println (identity (Box 7))
